C-a f opens any project, server or session
C-a b jumps back to the previous session
tm <host> opens an SSH session; C-b talks to the local tmux there
C-a z zooms the current pane, C-a z again restores it
C-a s shows every session and window with a preview
C-a ? shows the cheat sheet
C-a $ renames the current session
C-a , renames the current window
C-a [ starts copy mode: v selects, {{ if eq .profile "minimal" }}Enter{{ else }}y{{ end }} copies
Shift+drag selects text with the terminal instead of tmux
F12 hands all keys to a nested tmux
:set @tips off hides these tips
{{- if ne .profile "minimal" }}
C-a | and C-a - split the pane beside or below
C-a h/j/k/l moves between panes, C-a H/J/K/L resizes them
C-a < and C-a > move the current window left or right
Sessions are saved every 15 minutes and restored after a reboot
{{- end }}
